PHP 8.0 for Windows on arm64: php-src's Windows arm64 support, which landed
in 8.2, ported to 8.0.30 as pv builds it (after build/backports/php-8.0.list).
Applied by build/build-php-windows.sh with `git apply` before building.

Ported from these php-src commits:
  180557dd9c  Do not assert SSE/AVX resolvers at windows arm64
  745cf34ffc  Port standard/crc32 for windows arm64; NEWS and UPGRADING
              dropped. Windows defines no HAVE_AARCH64_CRC32, so this is
              inert there, as it is in 8.2
              (arm_acle.h guard adapted to 8.0's #if)
  02881a76a8  Port win32/codepage.c codes for windows arm64
  279a297172  Windows arm64 build system support; its fiber assembly and
              fiber build block dropped (no fibers before 8.1), and 8.0's
              toolset_setup_arch, which defines ARCHITECTURE rather than
              PHP_BUILD_ARCH, adapted by hand
  3a843f953b  Windows arm64 zend and standard extension support; the
              Zend/zend_atomic.h hunk dropped (no zend_atomic before 8.2), the
              json_encoder.c MSVC workaround adapted to 8.0's int return,
              and the string.c and base64.c NEON guards adapted by hand
  2be3aa86f0  gd's emmintrin.h on Windows arm64; its zend_vm_execute hunks
              do not apply, 8.0 having no execute_ex_real trampoline
  e2da6b4bf9  Use the default archive names for Windows ARM64 builds
  ca011bbf56  Drop unsupported libxml2 2.10.0 symbols (the docb* exports);
              needed because these lines link 8.2's arm64 libxml2 2.11.
              UPGRADING.INTERNALS dropped
  0c6fc66848  curl: add support for brotli and zstd on Windows, and
  1088c7de1a  Make curl brotli and zstd optional on Windows: 8.2's arm64
              libcurl links both; ext/curl/config.w32 as 8.2.35 has it

